## Endpoint read caching

Endpoint caching is disabled by default: each managed endpoint is read directly
through ERS. If Terraform manages many endpoints, enable caching to reduce
refresh requests:

```terraform
provider "ise" {
  endpoint_cache = true
}
```

Enabling caching loads the full paginated ISE endpoint inventory into memory on
the first eligible endpoint read in each provider session. Leave it disabled
when managing only a small subset of a large ISE inventory.

Bulk load errors and cache misses fall back to direct ERS reads. Imports use
direct reads to populate attributes omitted by the bulk API.

